From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: EE Cycle Rate goes down to -8 (21%) for the user to choose

On top of pcsx2-0005 (-4..-6). Guitar Hero (SLUS-21224) is held by its EE on
an RG52 Mini: measured second by second in a song, the emulated vsyncs a
second came to 57 on average at -6 (27%), the heavy parts at 49-51, and to 59
at -8 (21%), the heavy parts at 52-55, the first 40 s a flat 60; the game
plays right at -8 (the owner, 2026-11-02; dArkOS docs/KNOWN-ISSUES.md,
"Guitar Hero's speed"). -7 and -8 are offered as 24% and 21% Speed; the
recompiler's charge is the same formula, (5 - 2 * (rate + 1)) / 32 of a
block's cycles, and VU0's micro programs are charged the same ratio,
(5 - 2 * (rate + 1)) / 4. The governor still stops at -3.

